{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-325e9f4defcb53590ce4","statement":"[Theorem 1.1 of <<cite:DG>> and Theorem <<ref:main thm intro>>]\nThe quantum Hamiltonian reduction algebra $U_{-k,-C}$ has infinite global dimension in the following cases.\n\n- $k = \\frac{u}{v}$ for integers $1\\leq u<v\\leq n$.\n\n- There exist a partition $\\lambda\\in P_n$, an integer\n$0\\leq a \\leq \\ell-1$, and an integer\n$b\\not\\equiv 0 \\mod \\ell$ with $1\\leq b \\leq a + \\ell(\\on{ln}(\\lambda) -1)$ for which\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2b}{\\ell} - ([\\frac{b-a}{\\ell}]+1) = \\sum_{s=1}^b C_{a-b+s} -k(\\lambda_1-\\on{ln}(\\lambda))\n\\]\n\nIn all other cases, $U_{-k, -C}$ has finite global dimension, and hence derived microlocalization holds.","source_id":"arXiv:1108.6267","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"6773a3e32727f616b3a3178c0aa58d30e55f36c2b0dd3dc8c17ccf81fce8e3d7","kind":"corollary","label":"Corollary 61","ref_key":"cyclotomic global dimension","name":"","order":69,"deps":[{"ref":"main thm intro","card_id":"ma-c-86d78e1e8fba7b0a7d46","label":"Theorem 1","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":["DG"],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1108.6267","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"f70aa400f6c05f7aafe869bd2da6252e4a7c4f15ee66a6835e93994596be6e12","line":1728,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-26T15:09:23+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":614,"math_hints":49}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1108.6267","title":"Derived Equivalence for Quantum Symplectic Resolutions","abstract":"Using techniques from the homotopy theory of derived categories and noncommutative algebraic geometry, we establish a general theory of derived microlocalization for quantum symplectic resolutions. In particular, our results yield a new proof of derived Beilinson-Bernstein localization and a derived version of the more